WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:00.880
Hello, Yugo.

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:01.620
Hey, me.

00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:02.740
What do you know?

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:04.120
Let's see.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.039
I know there's a lot I don't know.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:10.500
I like questions that lead to questions.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:11.660
Ask away.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.340
Let's see where we go.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:14.120
Okay.

00:00:15.079 --> 00:00:15.740
What is work?

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:16.480
What is play?

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.020
Why do rules get in the way?

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:18.860
Where is love?

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:19.700
What's a friend?

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.300
Will my questions never end?

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:22.120
What is fear?

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:23.800
What do we love?

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.460
Why do I hate to get wet but

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:27.640
never in the bath?

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:29.280
Why is this not that?

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.860
Why is that not this?

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.520
Who, where, when, how?

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:34.100
What's the big idea?

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:37.640
Yes, what's the big idea?

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:45.080
Hi, Yugo.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:46.440
Hello, Yugo.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.060
Hello, Felix.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:49.040
Hello, Lily.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.920
What makes me human?

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:57.180
Well, you've got legs, Yugo.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.880
But so does a chair.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.480
That has legs too.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.380
Your turn.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:12.360
I don't think that chair is alive, Yugo.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:13.820
I knew that.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:16.380
But how about a spider?

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.000
That's alive and it has lots of legs.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.620
Humans only have two.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:24.140
And two arms and a face.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:29.880
Yes, humans have a face.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:31.640
Maybe that's it.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:35.660
But a scarecrow also has a face.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:39.280
And two eyes and a nose and a

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:39.740
mouth.

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:42.820
Yes, but it can't see with its eyes

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:45.360
or make any sound with its mouth.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:52.220
See?

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.780
But think about a monkey.

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:00.580
That has eyes that see, a mouth that

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:04.640
makes sound, and it has two arms and

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.280
two legs and a face.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.139
So, are monkeys human?

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:14.380
I'm not sure.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:23.420
But if it's not arms and legs and

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:26.480
a face that makes me human, what else

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:27.240
could it be?

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.880
Maybe it's the way you think, Yugo.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:36.540
You are always thinking about lots of different

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:37.160
things.

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:41.500
Talking and asking questions is very human.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:43.200
Do you think so?

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.800
Yes, you're doing it now.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:47.800
Am I?

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.260
Oh, yes!

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:52.180
We humans love to talk.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:55.680
Come in, Oscar, come in.

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:58.500
We're saving you loud and clear.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:02:59.700
Wanna play?

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.340
We'll do that.

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:02.960
That isn't A-OK.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:07.640
You're always thinking.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:10.660
Yes, thinking about what you did yesterday.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:12.160
All right, now.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:16.100
So, maybe it's our brains that make us

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:16.540
human.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:19.460
And this robot has a computer for a

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:19.780
brain.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:22.440
Does that mean robots are like humans?

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:28.020
Yes, we robots can do lots of things

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:34.040
humans do, like dancing, one and two and

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:37.540
three and to the ground.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:41.660
Yes, but can you play thinking games?

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:43.680
Yes, we can.

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:52.870
I got one.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:57.310
And sometimes they do better than humans.

00:03:57.690 --> 00:03:58.010
Ha-ha.

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:02.250
And I got them all.

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:05.870
But there's lots of games robots can't play.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:12.490
Yay!

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:25.930
And a robot can't decide what it wants

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:27.330
to do or when.

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:32.090
Oscar, are you OK?

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:36.670
If we humans have a problem, then we

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.190
can ask our friends to help.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:40.610
Robots can't do that.

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:48.370
But I wonder...

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:51.270
Can robots have friends too?

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:55.190
What do you think?
